body:
@tzhouam Yes, there are more people whose first name is Wijnand :wink:

@linzhenpl07 Thanks for drafting a plan already. I agree with your separation of memory-registry under #4480 and memory-allocator under #4366.

Mapping your phasing to what already exists: your P0 is, for the session-scoped part, #4480's Phase 0 — draft PR #4487 implements the registry (one `SessionMemoryManager` owning per-session state, lookup, lifecycle, and cleanup) and your own #4657 implements the request keying on top of it; the allocation mechanism your P2 would formalize merged with #4534; your P3 fork is implemented in draft PR #4909. What has no code today is the sessionless remainder of P0/P1, but I think it is out of scope here because your one-shot image gen use-case is not AR diffusion. So for the Q3 timeline I would order by what is closest to landing — #4487, then #4657, then #4480 Phase 1 (byte budget + a `PagedKV` handle over the engine state), then #4909 — and bring the registry/keying contract discussion to #4480, where the implementation already lives. Your registry introspection ideas (per-session objects and bytes, fork/eviction counts) would be a welcome extension there.
